sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Consumer
    actor Provider
    participant Service as Off-chain provider service
    participant Monitor as Selected monitor(s)
    participant Archive as Off-chain evidence archive
    participant Settle as SSESettlement
    actor Executor as Any Ethereum account
    Consumer->>Settle: admitEpoch(leaseId, requestHash)
    Settle-->>Consumer: epochId + deadlines + responseHash
    Monitor->>Service: HTTPS challenge and observation
    Service-->>Monitor: Service result / HTTP response (currently unsigned HTTP)
    Provider->>Settle: EIP-712 response commitment (relay permitted)
    Monitor->>Archive: Store raw observation and evidence
    Monitor->>Settle: EIP-712 verdict + evidence hash (or relayer)
    Note over Monitor,Settle: Three matching votes classify the current prototype outcome
    Executor->>Settle: sealMonitoring (after monitoringClose)
    Executor->>Settle: settleEpoch
    Settle->>Settle: Filter {N,F,S}; compute L, U and X
    Settle-->>Consumer: Credit f-U (pull withdrawal)
    Settle-->>Provider: Credit L (pull withdrawal)
    Note over Settle: Retain unresolved X, compensate only from separate budgets
    Executor->>Settle: closeEpochEvidence (after evidenceClose)
    opt Residual remains and parties sign an agreement (Phase 4 extension)
        Consumer-->>Executor: EIP-712 signature on exact residual split
        Provider-->>Executor: EIP-712 signature on same split
        Executor->>Settle: resolveResidualByAgreement(both signatures)
        Settle->>Settle: Validate split + signatures + one-shot replay guard
        Settle-->>Consumer: Agreed consumer credit
        Settle-->>Provider: Agreed provider credit
    end
